Comment (internal/service/migrator.go:369):
**Index dropped and recreated on every boot.** This `DROP INDEX IF EXISTS` + `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX` (no `IF NOT EXISTS`) runs unconditionally on every `MigrateUpWithConfig`, unlike the sibling `idx_dashboard_suggestions_unique_pending` directly above it (line 354) which uses `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS` and is genuinely idempotent.

Because this block isn't a versioned migration, every application startup drops and rebuilds this index. A non-`CONCURRENTLY` `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX` takes an `ACCESS EXCLUSIVE` lock (blocking reads/writes on `dashboard_suggestions` for the rebuild), and there's a brief window where the uniqueness guarantee is gone — exactly when a concurrently-booting instance or in-flight worker could insert a duplicate pending suggestion. The index is brand new in this PR, so there's no prior definition to replace.\n\nSuggest dropping the `DROP` and using `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS …` to match the sibling index. (Same change needed in the test migrator mirror.)
