**Empty-model fallback degenerates to `{_policy}` only — diverges from the documented default.** When the model omits `proposed_filter_labels` (`len(raw) == 0`), `normalized` is empty and the loop above adds nothing. The `_policy` injection at line 246 then runs *before* this `len(filterLabels) == 0` guard, so whenever the evidence has a `_policy` label, `filterLabels` is already `{_policy}` (len 1) and `defaultFilterLabelSubset` is **never reached**.

